    "note": "Claude Code ships with a small toolbox. Read opens a file. Write creates or overwrites a whole file. Edit swaps one exact piece of text. Bash runs commands. Grep searches what is inside files, while Glob finds files by their path or name. Most exploration mistakes come from mixing up those last two."
