    "note": "Glob answers which files exist, by name pattern. Grep answers which files mention something. Edit works by exact text match, and the old text must appear only once, so include a line or two of context to make it unique. If that fails, read the file and write it back in full. Current docs note that on Mac and Linux, search now runs through Bash by default."
