    "note": "Both approaches target part of the codebase. A CLAUDE dot md inside a folder is great when the convention belongs to that folder. But when the same convention applies to files scattered everywhere, like tests next to source code, a single path rule with a glob is cleaner. One source of truth, loaded only where it applies."
